    <briefdescription>
<para>Comparator that orders Macaulay-matrix column indices by the monomial each column represents, using the ambient <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monomial_info" kindref="compound">MonomialInfo</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Fed to <computeroutput>std::sort</computeroutput> so the F4 matrix builder can put the columns into the monoid&apos;s order before reduction. Keeps two static counters (<computeroutput><ref refid="class_columns_sorter_a3e1bf30c9fae9269c6ccda628222e433_1a3e1bf30c9fae9269c6ccda628222e433" kindref="member">ncmps</ref></computeroutput>, <computeroutput><ref refid="class_columns_sorter_a136349c50dc577574e2472a7f13d0bf2_1a136349c50dc577574e2472a7f13d0bf2" kindref="member">ncmps0</ref></computeroutput>) to let profiling code report how many comparisons the sort took. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
